  "development_type": "Major dwellings",
  "lapsed_date": "09/10/2010",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - The development hereby permitted shall be begun before the expiration of three years from the date of this permission.",
    "Condition : 2 - The materials to be used for the external surfaces of the extension hereby approved shall match those of the existing building.",
    "Condition : 3 - The office floorspace contained within the extension shall be used only as offices ancillary to the main use of the building for warehousing/industrial purposes and shall not be used for any other purpose.",
    "Condition : 4 - No additional floorspace/mezzanine shall be provided within the extended building, except the first floor floorspace approved as part of this development, without the prior approval in writing of the Local Planning Authority.",
    "Condition : 5 - The car and lorry parking spaces as shown on drawing P01 shall be provided and made available for use before occupation of any part of the extension hereby approved, and these spaces shall thereafter be retained and not used for any other purpose.",
    "Condition : 6 - a) The site shall be investigated for ground conditions, pollution, stability, landfill gas and leachate/ground water content/regime in accordance with details to be submitted to and shall be approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority before the development is implemented.b). The investigation shall be undertaken to the satisfaction of the Local Planning Authority and details of all results, assessments and measures needed to render the development safe in consequence, shall be submitted to and shall be approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority before the development is implemented. All such measures shall be implemented before the development is occupied or such other date as may be required by the Local Planning Authority.",
    "Condition : 7 - Full details of access and manoeuvrability for disabled persons within the site, including the ambulant disabled, shall be submitted to and shall be approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority before the development is commenced, and the development shall only be carried out in accordance with the approved details.",
    "Condition : 8 - Details of a planting scheme for the area between the eastern elevational wall of the extension and the site boundary to the east, shall be submitted to, and shall be approved in writing by, the Local Planning Authority prior to the commencement of the development. The approved details shall be implemented as approved on the first bringing into use of the extension, and the planting shall be maintained thereafter to the satisfaction of the Local Planning Authority."
  ],
